## Current Mock AI Behavior

The analyzer uses deterministic heuristics, not a paid model. It recognizes supported character nicknames and some contextual clues for new characters, locations, items, and Lore cards. Every create/update proposal remains pending until approved in Memory Review. Its phrase patterns are deliberately limited and may miss or misclassify ambiguous prose.

## Known Limitations

- The analyzer uses deterministic heuristics, not a real language model, and its evidence coverage remains intentionally limited.
- Entity discovery uses conservative deterministic name/context heuristics, not a language model; it can miss names and misclassify ambiguous phrases, so review approval remains required.
- Character nickname aliases resolve to their canonical cards; Lore discovery supports faction, creature, system, and concept cards but still uses limited phrase patterns.
- New Lore cards and their evidence-based updates are handled through Memory Review approval.
- The review panel has a bounded scroll area; resolved suggestions animate out of the pending list and remain in approved/rejected history. Verify the latest UX in the published browser app.
- The current provenance link is implemented for character-sheet updates first.
- `README.md` and `V2_SETUP.md` summarize current status, setup, deployment boundaries, and next steps. Keep them aligned as work proceeds.
- The mock login/testing bypass should eventually be removed or clearly isolated before real public use.
- Password recovery requires the deployed Marginalia URL to be allowed in Supabase Auth URL Configuration; live email delivery and password updates still need testing.
- The old `books.brain_dump` column remains for compatibility; new Brain Dumps are individual `documents` rows with `kind = 'brain_dump'`.
- The latest editor styles and rendered-row gutter have passed syntax/regression checks but have not yet been confirmed in the deployed site or visually smoke-tested across wrapping, font sizes, and mobile widths.

